/*
 * Kestrel - VP PACK (PC-B QUEUE 13 item 6): 8 voxel props imported from the committed CC0 "Voxel Pack" (MagicaVoxel,
 * design/vox-cc0/voxel-pack/, see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md "Voxel Pack (MagicaVoxel)" - CC0, attribution not required).
 * Feeds the owner's "Show it" showcase goal (forest/grassland shots, D-036): pig, bunny, bush, grass patch, campfire,
 * tree, stump, + one uncertain flat metal plate/icon (see its own desc below).
 *
 * Classic script (no import/export, check-deps rule 4), same loading convention as design/models/voxel_props.js:
 *   <script src="../design/models/vp_pack.js">     (browser, game/index.html - NOT yet wired in, see note below)
 *   import '../../../design/models/vp_pack.js';     (Node tests: side-effect import)
 * Sets ASSETS.voxelModels.<name> directly (format: architecture.md 15.1 VoxelModelDef). NOT yet added to
 * game/index.html's <script> list (shared hot file - PC-B main session's job, not this story's).
 *
 * PIPELINE: 4 raw multi-model .vox files (Raws.vox 30 models, Raws2.vox 30, Raws3.vox 12, RawsNumbers.vox 17 - the
 * last is a digit/UI set, not used here) were split with tools/vox-split.mjs into
 * design/vox-cc0/voxel-pack/split/<file>/<file>_NN.vox + index.json (per-model report: size, voxel count, bbox,
 * dominant colours, front/top ASCII projections). The source .vox carried NO MagicaVoxel scene/layer names
 * (sceneNodes: [] in every index.json), so each model below was identified by eye from its projection + colours,
 * not from an authoritative label - confidence noted per model in its own desc field.
 *
 * Each model was then converted with tools/vox-import.mjs (--map <palette index -> material key>, one map per
 * model, built interactively from vox-import's own "N palette index(es) used in the file are not mapped" error,
 * which lists every actually-used index - no guessing at the index set). Every material key used below ALREADY
 * EXISTS in design/palette.js materials (grep'd first) - no new palette/detail-pass entries were invented (that is
 * designer-owned shared data); where no close colour exists (pig hide, bunny nose, this pack's dark forest greens)
 * the closest existing hue is used and the mismatch is called out in that model's desc for the designer to revisit.
 *
 * All 8 models exceed the OLD hard limits (32/axis, 4096 voxels - every raw model here sits in a 20x20x20 or
 * 60x60x60 MagicaVoxel grid) but fit the ME-22 mesh-only bounds, so vox-import set voxel.meshOnly: true on all of
 * them automatically (mesh renderer only, architecture.md 28.12) - not fought, per this story's own instructions.
 *
 * --cell choices: 0.05 m/cell for pig/bush/campfire/stump (one shared human-scale unit), 0.02 m/cell for the
 * smaller bunny, 0.025 m/cell for the ground-hugging grass patch, 0.03 m/cell for the flat metal plate, and
 * 0.12 m/cell for the much bigger tree (60x60x60 grid, real height ~6 m) - sized per model from its own bbox
 * extents against a plausible real-world size (see each desc).
 *
 * NOT imported (scope note for a follow-up pass): the other ~81 split models in Raws/Raws2/Raws3/RawsNumbers
 * (a Player-looking humanoid walk cycle Raws_08-12, more pig/bunny animation frames Raws_13-19/Raws2_01-05, a lit
 * campfire variant Raws_28 and a different firepit-with-embers Raws3_07/08, assorted tiny unidentified props, and
 * all 17 RawsNumbers digit/UI models) - their split .vox + index.json already exist under
 * design/vox-cc0/voxel-pack/split/ for whoever picks that up next; no need to re-run vox-split.
 */
